## Comparing Two Sets

Set A minus Set B gives you everything in A that is NOT in B. This is called the **set difference**.

### Computing Difference Manually

```xiom
fn set_difference(a_set: &Set[Str], b_set: &Set[Str], a_items: &Vec[Str]) -> Vec[Str] {
  let result: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
  let i = 0;
  while i < a_items.len() {
    let item = match a_items.get(i) { Some(v) => v, None => "" };
    if !b_set.contains(&item) {
      result.push(item);
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }
  return result;
}
```

### Finding Common Items: Intersection

```xiom
fn set_intersection(a_set: &Set[Str], b_set: &Set[Str], a_items: &Vec[Str]) -> Vec[Str] {
  let result: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
  let i = 0;
  while i < a_items.len() {
    let item = match a_items.get(i) { Some(v) => v, None => "" };
    if b_set.contains(&item) {
      result.push(item);
    }
    i = i + 1;
  }
  return result;
}
```

The only difference between these functions: `!b_set.contains(&item)` vs `b_set.contains(&item)`. One `!` changes "not in" to "in".

### Putting It All Together

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let my_movies: Set[Str] = Set[Str].new();
  my_movies.insert("Inception");
  my_movies.insert("Matrix");
  my_movies.insert("Interstellar");
  let my_list: Vec[Str] = Vec[Str].new();
  my_list.push("Inception"); my_list.push("Matrix"); my_list.push("Interstellar");

  let friend_movies: Set[Str] = Set[Str].new();
  friend_movies.insert("Matrix");
  friend_movies.insert("Avatar");

  let only_i_saw = set_difference(&my_movies, &friend_movies, &my_list);
  io.println("Only I've seen: " + string.int_to_str(only_i_saw.len()));

  let both_saw = set_intersection(&my_movies, &friend_movies, &my_list);
  io.println("We both saw: " + string.int_to_str(both_saw.len()));
  return 0;
}
```

### The Three Core Set Operations

| Operation | Meaning | Result |
|-----------|---------|--------|
| Difference (A - B) | In A, not in B | `!b.contains(x)` |
| Intersection (A n B) | In both A and B | `b.contains(x)` |
| Union (A u B) | In A or B | `result.push(x)` from both |

